 ## Help Parameter Customization
 
-Help parameters are automatically added by Click for any command. The default is `--help` but can be overridden by the context setting {attr}`~Context.help_option_names`. Click also performs automatic conflict resolution on the default help parameter, so if a command itself implements a parameter named `help` then the default help will not be run.
+Help parameters are automatically added by Click for any command. The default is `--help` but can be overridden by the context setting {attr}`~Context.help_option_names`. If a command explicitly declares an option with one of these flags, that flag is reserved for the user option. Any remaining help flags are still available.
+
+A parameter's internal name does not override a help flag. For example, an
+argument named `help`, or an option declared as `@click.option("--value", "help")`,
+can coexist with the automatic `--help` option. Click chooses a distinct internal
+name for the automatic help option when needed.
 
 This example changes the default parameters to `-h` and `--help`
 instead of just `--help`:
